{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 11: is the plant worth it at 1% a month? Construction spending for 10 months, then a margin that ramps up, over a 10-year horizon. Present value is kept as a stock of discounted cash. }
Construction Cost=
	3e+06
	~	dollars
	~	|
Construction Time=
	10
	~	month
	~	|
Construction Spending=
	IF THEN ELSE(Time < Construction Time, Construction Cost / Construction Time, 0)
	~	dollars/month
	~	Spent evenly while the plant is built.
	|
Plant Available=
	STEP(1, Construction Time)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Ramp Up Time=
	6
	~	month
	~	Average time to reach full output once the plant is built.
	|
Ramp Up=
	(Plant Available - Utilisation) / Ramp Up Time
	~	1/month
	~	|
Utilisation= INTEG(
	Ramp Up,
	0)
	~	dmnl
	~	Fraction of full output reached.
	|
Full Margin=
	60000
	~	dollars/month
	~	Monthly margin at full output.
	|
Margin=
	Full Margin * Utilisation
	~	dollars/month
	~	|
Cash Flow=
	Margin - Construction Spending
	~	dollars/month
	~	|
Cumulative Cash= INTEG(
	Cash Flow,
	0)
	~	dollars
	~	Undiscounted: what an accountant's running total shows.
	|
Discount Rate=
	0.01
	~	1/month
	~	Continuous rate per month.
	|
Discount Factor=
	EXP(-Discount Rate * Time)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Discounted Cash Flow=
	Cash Flow * Discount Factor
	~	dollars/month
	~	Each month's cash, valued today.
	|
Present Value= INTEG(
	Discounted Cash Flow,
	0)
	~	dollars
	~	The value today of the cash flows so far: a stock of discounted cash.
	|
Built In NPV=
	NPV(Cash Flow, Discount Rate, 0, 1)
	~	dollars
	~	The same quantity from the simulator's own function.
	|
Annual Return=
	INTERNAL RATE OF RETURN(Cash Flow, 12, 0)
	~	1/year
	~	The rate per year (compounded yearly) that makes the cash flows so far worth nothing today. Read per 12 months because the per-month form fails on long runs (see the notes).
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ month ~ |
FINAL TIME = 120 ~ month ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
